   "subject": "Updating simulation attributes using a function",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Hi.<p>I am trying to update an attribute using a function called to update/set another attribute. Is it possible?<p>A simple hypothetical example:<p>set_attribute(keys = &quot;hieght&quot;,<br>              values = function(){<br>temp = rnorm(1, 1.7, 0.15)<br>set_attribute(keys = &quot;weight&quot;,<br>              values = temp - 100)<br>temp<br>})</p></p></p>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "dAjLn6TCFgAJ",
   "from": "Iñaki Ucar",
   "author": "0f5b7adb7e70bd8b",
   "date": "2019-08-10T09:39:52Z",
   "subject": "Re: [simmer-devel] Updating simulation attributes using a function",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "You can set several attributes at once. Please, see the examples\r<br>section under help(set_attribute).\r<br>\r<br>Iñaki\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "\r<br>On Sat, 10 Aug 2019 at 10:45, Wael MOHAMMED &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">mrwaelm...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; Hi.\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; I am trying to update an attribute using a function called to update/set another attribute. Is it possible?\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; A simple hypothetical example:\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; set_attribute(keys = &quot;hieght&quot;,\r<br>&gt;               values = function(){\r<br>&gt; temp = rnorm(1, 1.7, 0.15)\r<br>&gt; set_attribute(keys = &quot;weight&quot;,\r<br>&gt;               values = temp - 100)\r<br>&gt; temp\r<br>&gt; })\r<br>&gt;\r<br>"
    ],
